  "_comment": [
    "ICT Form 3 Teacher’s Guide, first typeset 2026-11-23 from \"ICT Form 3 - Teachers Book - V9 - FINAL - Ready for Typesetting 23 Nov REVISED.docx\".",
    "Subject spelled \"Information and Communications Technology\" as on the manuscript title and as the ICT Form 3 LB sets it (theme default reads Communication), so cover, title page and running header agree across the pair.",
    "authors: the publisher line under the author on the manuscript title page was picked up as a second author; the guide has one author.",
    "Topic 3.4 restarts Learning Activity / Exercise numbers at Specific Competence 3.4.1.2, as the LB does: left as written.",
    "End of Topic answer guides: each sat in a one-column Word frame (now unwrapped by the engine). Their titles and the \"Marking guide: Section A/B\" lines are set as heads, so none is left at a page foot apart from its table.",
    "image9 (Figure TG 3.1.6, site map): the white margin round the drawing trimmed (ICT Form 3 TG-art/site-map-trimmed.png) so the last lines of Topic 3.1 do not run onto a page of their own before Topic 3.2.",
    "boxAllRows: the activity and exercise boxes are one-column Word tables whose later rows hold the model-answer tables and figures (Table TG 3.1.1 ... Figure TG 3.4.4); without it only each box’s first row printed and 25 of them were missing.",
    "subtext: nine Expected responses items typed with no space after the number (\"2.The organisation’s name\"), unlike the rest of their lists.",
    "image7 (Figure TG 3.1.4, page sketch) a little narrower so it stays in Learning Activity 4 under the line that introduces it instead of leaving half of page 17 empty.",
    "Proofreading round 1 (24 Nov 2026): every Learner’s Book page reference set to the typeset LB (round 1 build, PR #239): Learning Activity / Exercise pages read from the LB itself, ranges as the reviewer gave them (the two agree throughout). The edit/editCell entries are generated so each matches exactly once in the order the engine applies them.",
    "tableWidths (new key, round 1): Table TG I.2 Level column wide enough for \"Comprehension\"; Table TG 3.1.1 \"Coding needed?\" / \"Templates available\" no longer run together; Appendix 3 \"No.\" apart from \"Learner’s name\"; Resource Sheet 4 phone numbers on one line.",
    "Kept as the house rule has it: the \"Model answer:\" label before \"SaaS – Gmail…\" (house style marks an answer by italic on its own line, never by a label). Table TG A.8 now opens with its caption; nothing to do.",
    "Appendices 1-4 listed in the contents under APPENDICES (as in the V9 contents; reviewer suggestion): their heads set as h2.",
    "Round 2 fix-everything (24 Nov 2026): subtext for a stray \"write]\", one serial comma (house rule), the one lesson heading not in title case, \"Evaluation/ Communication\" (not a cognitive level; Q5 produces a message: Creation), \"Questions 2(a) and 2(b)\" in Figure TG 3.2.4, and Exercise 6 Discussion 2 (\"as happened last term\" said the opposite of the scenario). editCell: the acronym list and lesson-plan Subject now read \"Communications\" like the rest of the book (the 2024 syllabus title in the Foreword and References is that document’s own name, left as is); \"password\" as in the Expected responses.",
    "setHeading h2: the Introduction’s \"Assessments\" section (the engine no longer boxes a Heading-styled Assessment(s) before the first topic) and the four \"End of Topic 3.x Assessment\" headings, so the contents lists them as the V9 contents does."
